-- title:
--   Box sheet is a fundamental domain for rational unipotent points
-- statement:
--   The statement concerns the group $G = \mathrm{GL}_3$ over the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$, the adeles and the general linear group both carrying their Borel $\sigma$-algebras. Let $N$ be `unipotentSubgroup3`, the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ generated by all matrices $n(x,y,z)$ with $1$ on the diagonal, $x$, $y$, $z$ in positions $(1,2)$, $(2,3)$, $(1,3)$ and zeros below the diagonal, equipped with the measure `unipotentHaar3` obtained by pushing the threefold product of the additive Haar measure of $\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}$ forward along $(x,y,z) \mapsto n(x,y,z)$. Let $\Gamma = N \cap \mathrm{image}$ of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q})$ under the map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}$, and let $T \subseteq N$ consist of those elements whose matrix is $n(x,y,z)$ with $x$, $y$, $z$ each in the adelic box of $\mathbb{Q}$ (infinite part in the preimage of the fundamental parallelotope of the lattice basis of the Minkowski space, finite part integral at every finite place). Then: $\Gamma$ is countable; $T$ is measurable; $T$ is a fundamental domain for $\Gamma$, viewed as a subgroup of $N$, acting on $N$; for every measurable $F : N \to [0,\infty]$ the integral of $F$ over $T$ equals the iterated integral of $F(n(x,y,z))$ over three copies of the box against additive adelic Haar measure, and also equals the cube of the Haar measure of the box times the corresponding iterated integral against the Haar measure conditioned on the box; and the measure of $T$ is the cube of the measure of the box.
--
--   This is the unipotent analogue, in rank three, of the reduction theory statement that a product of fundamental boxes for $\mathbb{Q} \subset \mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q}$ gives a fundamental domain for the rational points of the upper triangular unipotent group acting on its adelic points, together with the resulting Fubini formula for integrals over that domain. It supplies the measure-theoretic input for [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_pos_lt_top_lintegral_slab_eq_mul_pow_three_mul_lintegral_quotientMeasure`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_pos_lt_top_lintegral_slab_eq_mul_pow_three_mul_lintegral_quotientMeasure), where integrals over the unipotent slab are converted into integrals against normalised measures on the quotient.
